#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""MiniCut Patch 39 - Adaptive Proxy (baked preview segments, experimental, off by default)

* Heavy parts of the timeline (many clips, effects, masks) are rendered once in the background into small All-Intra files and played from them. Preview only; export never uses them. Switch on in Settings.
* Segments are LIVE, DIRTY, BAKING or BAKED, ordered by a cost score. Proxies are S / M / L / XL (2 s, 6 s, 18 s, 54 s) with idle merge S>M, M>L, L>XL by stream copy.
* A proxy is used only when the content hash of its time range matches (clips, effects, keyframes, tracks, node graph, source files, effect code). An edit makes only the ranges it touches stale; Undo finds the old proxy again; a stale merged proxy is split back into its unchanged parts.
* One bake at a time, only when idle, dropped at once when you edit, never during export; a half-made file is never used. Cache limit 2 GB, files older than 30 days are removed. Folder: .minicut/bake in your user folder.

Files changed: minicut/app.py, minicut/render/export.py, minicut/render/renderer.py, minicut/shared/core.py, minicut/shared/dialogs.py, minicut/workspace/viewport.py, minicut/render/bake.py
  python Patch/apply_39_adaptive_proxy.py --check      (look only, change nothing)
  python Patch/apply_39_adaptive_proxy.py              (install)
  python Patch/apply_39_adaptive_proxy.py --revert     (put the files back from the backup)
Close MiniCut before installing. The MiniCut Launcher can do all of this for you.
"""
import base64, datetime, hashlib, json, os, py_compile, shutil, sys, zlib
